  data:  # 9dfc
    kind: work_item  # 9dfc
    title: "php: double-quoted Laravel route paths silently undetected (encapsed_string vs string)"  # 9dfc
    status: todo_hard  # 9dfc
    priority: 2  # 9dfc
    parent:  # 9dfc
    tags:  # 9dfc
    - wave5  # 9dfc
    - route  # 9dfc
    isbefore: []  # 9dfc
    duplicate_of: []  # 9dfc
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 9dfc
    pr_ref:  # 9dfc
    description: "php.py `_extract_laravel_routes` extracts the route path only from tree-sitter `string`\nnodes and never from `encapsed_string`, so every DOUBLE-QUOTED Laravel route path is\nsilently undetected. Single quotes work.\n\nLive repro (2026-07-29), PHPAnalyzer directly on a 3-line fixture:\n\n    <?php\n    Route::get(\"/users\", [UserController::class, \"index\"]);   // NOT detected\n    Route::post('/users', [UserController::class, 'store']);  // detected\n\n  symbols: 2\n    php:routes.php:1-1:file:file            (the file node)\n    php:routes.php:3-3:POST /users:route    (only the single-quoted one)\n\nParse tree confirms the cause: a double-quoted PHP literal is `encapsed_string`\n(children: `\"`, `string_content`, `\"`), a single-quoted one is `string`. The arg\nwalk tests `arg_child.type == \"string\"` and falls through on `encapsed_string`.\nThe docstring's own examples are all single-quoted, so the gap was never visible\nfrom the module's own documentation.\n\nDouble-quoted paths are idiomatic and common in Laravel, so this is a real\nroute-detection coverage hole (WI-tosul family), not a cosmetic one. Same class of\ndefect as WI-zunal's `Route::match` drop: an unsupported literal shape silently\ndrops the whole route rather than degrading it.\n\nFix shape: accept `encapsed_string` wherever `string` is accepted for route-path\nand controller-action args. Check the shared helper `_php_string_value` first --\nif it already handles both, the call sites are bypassing it, which makes this a\nchokepoint fix rather than a per-site one. Also sweep the other php arg walks\n(resource/apiResource/match) for the same literal-type assumption.\n\nFound while building route-parity fixtures for WI-zugob (the php fixture emitted\nzero markers, which is what surfaced it)."  # 9dfc
    fields: {}  # 9dfc
- op: discuss  # 2d26
  at: '2026-10-01T00:57:30Z'  # 2d26
  by: agent  # 2d26
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 2d26
  clock: 2  # 2d26
  nonce: 2d26  # 2d26
  message: "PREMISE CHECK 2026-09-30 (dev 7f0f993843): CURRENT-WITH-UPDATES.\nCause holds: php.py _extract_laravel_routes still tests `arg_child.type == \"string\"` for the route path (now php.py:803). No commit since filing touched it (git log -S encapsed_string on php.py: last 686aa99c2c, 2026-04-15).\nLive repro (analyze_php on a 6-line scratch fixture): of Route::get(\"/users\",...), Route::post('/users',...), Route::match(['get','post'], \"/m\",...), Route::resource(\"photos\", PhotoController::class), Route::get(\"/u/{$x}\",...) ONLY the single-quoted POST /users emitted a route symbol. So double quotes drop match and resource routes too, not only get/post.\nDrift: the route marker's kind slot is now `function` (meta.framework_role=route), not `:route` as the repro output in the description shows.\nChokepoint answer to the item's question: _php_string_value (php.py:499) reads the first `string_content` child, which an encapsed_string also has; the call site at :803 bypasses it by its type test. _extract_controller_action already accepts encapsed_string (:591 array-action arm, marked `# pragma: no cover` = untested; :607 'C@a' arm). _laravel_collect_string_args/_laravel_extract_strings (:714, only/except) already accept both.\nSame-literal-type sweep, one more site: _laravel_match_methods (php.py:541) accepts only `string` for the verb array, so Route::match([\"get\",\"post\"], ...) degrades to the MATCH aggregate (degrades, not dropped).\nDesign point the fix must decide: an interpolated path \"/u/{$x}\" is an encapsed_string with variable children; _php_string_value would return only its first string_content (\"/u/\"), a truncated path. Refuse or mark such a path; do not emit the prefix as the route.\nNot checked: frequency on a real Laravel corpus repo."  # 2d26
- op: update  # f98f
