  message: "DONE: merged in PR #1383. _php_string_value is the single string reader for the Laravel argument walk: both quote styles, whole-string escape decoding, None for interpolated strings (callers refuse). On the item's fixture: before, only POST /users (+ a MATCH /n aggregate); after, GET /users (UserController@index), GET,POST /m, the 7 photos resource routes and GET,POST /n; \"/u/{$x}\" emits nothing rather than /u/; '/it\\'s' no longer reads as /it. Tests: TestLaravelDoubleQuotedRoutes (9) + TestPhpStringValue (20 cases); the red phase was shown by live repro, not a recorded failing test run. koel (the corpus's only Laravel repo, single-quoted) unchanged: 167 markers / 111 contexts, so measured corpus effect is zero. Residuals: WI-sitag, WI-jodoh (P3).\nFull report (closure evidence, corpus tables, residual list): /home/jgstern_agent/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/decontend/run_09302026/fadip.md"  # 4742
